  "rewrites": {
   "5": {
    "original": "The unique debut published under the title, Too much busyness raises my doubts (yehovitigena mahapravesha pitey... ), attempts to elevate Martin Luther King Jr. and Mahatma Gandhi to the status of IT people during India's independence movement and points out how the two would proceed with their activities.",
    "rewrite": "The singular first release titled, Excessive(busyness) casts doubt (yehovitigena mahapravesha pitey)..., seeks to position Martin Luther King Jr. and Mahatma Gandhi as IT professionals during India\u2019s struggle for independence and highlights their approach to action."
   },
   "4": {
    "original": "Thinking what would Martin Luther King Jr. and Mahatma Gandhi do if they worked in an IT firm, an official from the Mysore press club and former journalist, Bhavyavarma Prabhakar, has penned down in a collection of essays.",
    "rewrite": "An official from the Mysore press club and former journalist, Bhavyavarma Prabhakar, has written a collection of essays titled \"If Martin Luther King Jr. and Mahatma Gandhi Worked in an IT Firm and Were Confronted with Modern Challenges.\""
   },
   "6": {
    "original": "On a personal note, I lost a friend (sadly, since 2004) and I pray... nah, I'm very sure I won't but request and send my thoughts, if it's contrary to their right path. three good time...",
    "rewrite": "On a personal note, I lost a friend in 2004 and often pray..., although I am rather confident that is not the case, but I will send my thoughts requesting they stay on the right path. It has been a wonderful time..."
   },
   "9": {
    "original": "With both of us too busy this week, we had time to play just once with the new bass player of the jazz combo I'm playing with.",
    "rewrite": "Because we were both occupied this week, we managed to play only once with the new bass player in the jazz combo I am in."
   },
   "8": {
    "original": "I've become a fan of \"jam sessions\" ever since I heard Armando's Jazz kidnap (2CD) from itunes earlier last year.",
    "rewrite": "I've developed an appreciation for \"jam sessions\" after hearing Armando's Jazz (2CD) on itunes from that time last year."
   },
   "13": {
    "original": "Cassandra Kates had spent a few months on observing one of the world's busiest public transport systems.",
    "rewrite": "Cassandra Kates dedicated several months to observing one of the globe's most crowded public transportation networks."
   },
   "2": {
    "original": "It will be cool to have anyone on the planet type my birthdays on this board!",
    "rewrite": "It would be exciting to see anyone in the world enter my birthdays on this board!"
   },
   "1": {
    "original": "Google announced an interactive tabletop called Think Board.",
    "rewrite": "Google launched an interactive tabletop known as Think Board."
   },
   "11": {
    "original": "Later, maybe we would try the Super Bowl music video!",
    "rewrite": "Later on, perhaps we could attempt the Super Bowl music video!"
   }
  },
  "final_span": "of stealing Internet technology!\nGoogle launched an interactive tabletop known as Think Board. It would be exciting to see anyone in the world enter my birthdays on this board!\nBreakaway daydream\nAn official from the Mysore press club and former journalist, Bhavyavarma Prabhakar, has written a collection of essays titled \"If Martin Luther King Jr. and Mahatma Gandhi Worked in an IT Firm and Were Confronted with Modern Challenges.\"\nThe singular first release titled, Excessive(busyness) casts doubt (yehovitigena mahapravesha pitey)..., seeks to position Martin Luther King Jr. and Mahatma Gandhi as IT professionals during India\u2019s struggle for independence and highlights their approach to action.\nOn a personal note, I lost a friend in 2004 and often pray..., although I am rather confident that is not the case, but I will send my thoughts requesting they stay on the right path. It has been a wonderful time...\nEarlier posted here.\nI've developed an appreciation for \"jam sessions\" after hearing Armando's Jazz (2CD) on itunes from that time last year. Because we were both occupied this week, we managed to play only once with the new bass player in the jazz combo I am in.\nSome videos taken from Jam Session with in a restaurant bar in Longyearbyen, Svalbard, Norway;\nLater on, perhaps we could attempt the Super Bowl music video!\nDavid Boaz keeps warning the next Alexandria Ocasiocrazy, Swat valley manacer at large or I'm reminded of my Nip and tuck wrath towards, Joel Filartiga for a \"Cause of action against gun violence is the freedom of information\"\nCassandra Kates dedicated several months to observing one of the globe's most crowded public transportation networks. She mentions in her entry, \"Every time I got off the train I felt: I wonder what my life would be like if I took the train every day.\" And suggests \"over time the elevator became a microcosm of my life.\"\nI'll make one big decision in the next couple",
  "break_point": null
 },
